Feature: LiveView declarations
  Views declare their entity once; events shrink to the permission.

  Scenario: Shorthand authorize uses the module default
    Given a LiveView declared "edict_entity :project, from: :project_id"
    When it declares 'authorize "delete", :delete'
    Then the "delete" event is guarded with permission "delete" on entity type "project" from assign "project_id"

  Scenario: A list of events shares one declaration
    Given a LiveView declared "edict_entity :project, from: :project_id"
    When it declares 'authorize ["save", "publish"], :write'
    Then the "save" and "publish" events are guarded with permission "write" on entity type "project"

  Scenario: An undeclared literal event fails compilation
    Given a LiveView with handle_event clauses for "save" and "ping"
    And only "save" is authorized
    When the LiveView compiles
    Then compilation fails naming "ping" and both remedies

  Scenario: An event listed in unguarded_events compiles
    Given a LiveView with handle_event clauses for "save" and "validate"
    And "save" is authorized and "validate" is listed in unguarded_events
    When the LiveView compiles
    Then it compiles

  Scenario: A macro-generated event is checked
    Given a LiveView whose handle_event clause for "ping" is generated by a macro
    And "ping" is not declared
    When the LiveView compiles
    Then compilation fails naming "ping"

  Scenario: An undeclared pinned literal event fails compilation
    Given a LiveView with a handle_event clause matching "save" = event
    And "save" is not declared
    When the LiveView compiles
    Then compilation fails naming "save"

  Scenario: An event authorized twice fails compilation
    When a LiveView authorizes "save" in two declarations
    Then compilation fails naming "save"

  Scenario: An event listed twice in unguarded_events fails compilation
    When a LiveView lists "validate" twice in unguarded_events
    Then compilation fails naming "validate"

  Scenario: An event declared both ways fails compilation
    When a LiveView authorizes "save" and lists it in unguarded_events
    Then compilation fails naming "save"

  Scenario: A dynamic event name compiles
    Given a LiveView with a handle_event clause matching any event name
    When the LiveView compiles
    Then it compiles
